      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and I can't think of a clinical setting where it would be appropriate. It risks acute liver failure, and a 70 kg patient with normal liver function has no extra margin. Entering it as written could seriously harm your patient.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a safe dose now.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. I can add a note capping the total at 4 g/day.\n- **Call pharmacy or your attending.** They can review the intent behind the order. If a different drug or route was meant, they can help sort that out.\n- **Consider whether this is a unit mix-up.** Maybe you meant 500 mg, or a different drug.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you want, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
